<title>USA: AMR orders seats from BE Aerospace, others.</title>
<headline>AMR orders seats from BE Aerospace, others.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Airlines, a unit of AMR Corp, said Monday it has contracted to buy more than 70,000 aircraft seats valued at more than $268 million.</p>
<p>It said it will buy the customized seats from U.S.-based BE Aerospace Inc and Weber Aircraft and Germany's Recaro.</p>
<p>The seats will be used in American's first, business and coach class aircraft and most will be installed by the year 2000, it said.</p>
